Fix a missing build dependency that causes a non-deterministic ninja
parallel-build race.

gdk/broadway/meson.build declares the gtk4-broadwayd executable's
sources without including the generated gdkversionmacros_h header,
even though broadway-server.c transitively includes
gdk/version/gdkversionmacros.h (via gdktypes.h -> gdkenums.h). Because
ninja has no declared edge between the header-generating custom_target
and this compile, it is free to schedule the compile before the header
is generated, causing an intermittent build failure:

  fatal error: gdk/version/gdkversionmacros.h: No such file or directory

The static library target in the same file already lists the full
gdk_gen_headers (which includes gdkversionmacros_h) as sources and
does not race. Add gdkversionmacros_h to the executable's sources so
ninja orders it correctly as well.

diff --git a/gdk/broadway/meson.build b/gdk/broadway/meson.build
index 1579c1fda5..6267111674 100644
--- a/gdk/broadway/meson.build
+++ b/gdk/broadway/meson.build
@@ -72,6 +72,7 @@ executable('gtk4-broadwayd',
     broadwayjs_h,
     gdkconfig,
     gdkenum_h,
+    gdkversionmacros_h,
     'broadwayd.c',
     'broadway-server.c',
     'broadway-output.c',
